{"name":"God-Given","hex":"#faf4e0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"god","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Godié."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deity or supreme being; a supernatural, typically immortal, being with superior powers, to which personhood is attributed.","An idol.\nA representation of a deity, especially a statue or statuette.\n Something or someone particularly revered, worshipped, idealized, admired and/or followed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/god"},{"term":"given","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of give"]},{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["Considering; taking into account."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/given"}],"entries":[{"title":"Year Zero (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Year Zero is the fifth studio album by the American industrial rock band Nine Inch Nails, released by Interscope Records on April 17, 2007. Conceived while touring in support of the band's previous album, With Teeth (2005), the album was recorded in late 2006. It was produced by Trent Reznor and Atticus Ross, and was the band's first studio album since 1994's The Downward Spiral that was not co-produced by long-time collaborator Alan Moulder. It was the band's last album for Interscope until the Tron: Ares soundtrack in 2025, following Reznor's departure after the album's release due to a dispute regarding overseas pricing."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/02/Nine_Inch_Nails_-_Year_Zero.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Year_Zero_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9f/Nine_inch_nails_year_zero_cd_face.jpg/330px-Nine_inch_nails_year_zero_cd_face.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9f/Nine_inc